A `#[go.native]` type may be the only mention its package gets.

A native *function* registers its import where the call is emitted, which is
enough while every mention of the package is a call. A native *type* is spelled
by `IRTypeToGo`, a free function with no context to register anything from --
and a var of one becomes a field, a getter and a setter that name the package
with nothing calling into it beside them.

This program is that shape: `arm` is never called on either target, so the only
`time.` in the output is the type. Without the import the package did not
compile at all -- `undefined: time` -- which a golden alone would not have
shown, since the text looks right.

A *field* of a native type is the same claim one level in, and is why the walk
does not stop at a program's own struct: `Box` holds a `Vals`, and the Go
struct emitted for it spells `url.Values` with nothing else in the file naming
that package either.

`BaseImports` is where it is collected, off the *values* a package declares
rather than off `pkg.Structs`: a platform package's own type is not in a
program's struct list, and fyne's `Schedule` reaches a program only as the type
of the `handle` var its timer override declares. All three Go platforms already
ask `BaseImports` for the scheme imports, so none grew a case.

The import line itself is what the goldens below show; that it *compiles* is
the per-platform harness's claim, which builds every testdata fixture for its
own target and is where the missing import surfaced.

deny * `t__inst\d+ +Ticker` -- the field is the Go type the mark names, not the SNGL name
deny * `\*time\.Ticker\{\}` -- a pointer type has no composite literal
deny * `(?m)^\tM Vals$` -- a native-typed field is the Go type the mark names

-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"
import go "sngl:language/go"

#[go.native("time", "*time.Ticker")]
struct Ticker {}

#[go.native("time", "time.NewTicker")]
func arm(d int) Ticker

#[go.native("net/url", "url.Values")]
struct Vals {}

output {
    go {
        fyne
        bubbletea
    }
}

struct Box {
    m Vals
}

component main ui.node {
    var t Ticker
    var boxes list<Box> = []

    ui.text(value=string(boxes.length()))
}

ui.window(title="import") { main }
-- out/go/bubbletea/model.go --
